Hello,

Can we add support in MAVSDK for sending STATUSTEXT messages to the GCS?

Currently, I have an application with it's own logger class that prints to console. 
When there are errors, I want these to show up on the GCS using the STATUSTEXT messages.

Here is my current implementation using MAVSDK. MAV_SEVERITY is from the mavlink common header file.

```
void Autonomy::send_statustext(MAV_SEVERITY severity, const std::string msg)
{
    auto chunk_statustext = [](const std::string& msg) -> std::vector<std::string>
    {
        constexpr size_t MAX_LEN = 50;

        std::vector<std::string> chunks;

        size_t i = 0;
        while (i < msg.size())
        {
            size_t remaining = msg.size() - i;

            if (remaining >= MAX_LEN)
            {
                // Full chunk, no room for null terminator
                chunks.emplace_back(msg.substr(i, MAX_LEN));
                i += MAX_LEN;
            }
            else
            {
                // Last chunk — must include null terminator
                std::string last = msg.substr(i, remaining);
                last.push_back('\0');  // MAVLink uses this to signal final chunk
                chunks.emplace_back(std::move(last));
                break;
            }
        }

        // Edge case: empty string → send a single null-terminated chunk
        if (chunks.empty())
        {
            chunks.emplace_back(std::string(1, '\0'));
        }

        return chunks;
    };

    auto chunks = chunk_statustext(msg);

    auto uid = []() {
        static std::atomic<uint16_t> counter{1};
        uint16_t id = counter++;
        if (id == 0) id = counter++; // skip 0
        return id;
    };

    uint16_t id = (chunks.size() > 1) ? uid() : 0;

    for (size_t i = 0; i < chunks.size(); ++i)
    {
        MavlinkDirect::MavlinkMessage status_txt_msg{};
        status_txt_msg.message_name = "STATUSTEXT";

        nlohmann::json fields;
        fields["severity"] = severity;

        // Pad to exactly 50 bytes
        std::string text = chunks[i];
        text.resize(50, '\0');

        fields["text"] = text;
        fields["id"] = id;
        fields["chunk_seq"] = static_cast<uint8_t>(i);

        status_txt_msg.fields_json = fields.dump();
        std::cout << status_txt_msg.fields_json << std::endl;

        {
            std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(this->mux_queue);
            this->message_queue.push(status_txt_msg);
        }
    }
}

```

Is this supported in MAVSDK? Perhaps @bansiesta can help us figure out if this is currently supported, and if not, create a new pull request for it? 
It would be good to preserve the chunking feature.

